iamf-sentinel-pro
Copyright 2026 The iamf-sentinel authors

This product includes software developed as original, clean-room
implementations: the BS.1770-4 loudness / true-peak measurement (dsp.py
and the sentinel-dsp C++ kernel) written from ITU-R BS.1770-4; the ADM
source-referenced comparison's BW64/chna/axml reader written from
ITU-R BS.2088 and EBU Tech 3285; and the ISO-BMFF handling written from
ISO/IEC 14496-12. No AOM reference-decoder or reference-encoder source
code is used or derived. Reference decoders (decoder_main, iamfdec) and
EAR (ear-render) are invoked strictly as subprocess oracles across CLI
boundaries. numpy (BSD-licensed) is an optional dependency.

